; `pi install <package>` runs `npm install --omit=dev` in the package
; directory, and npm reads this file from there.
;
; rho bundles extensions whose declared peer ranges name old pi versions
; (token-rate-pi asks for @earendil-works/pi-ai ^0.74.0). no pi that rho can
; run satisfies those ranges, so npm's peer resolution fails and the whole
; install aborts before any script runs. peer resolution has nothing to
; resolve here in any case: pi's packages are not fetched from the registry,
; they are symlinked to the installed pi by tools/link-pi-packages.ts, so that
; a class imported by an extension is the class pi instantiates.
legacy-peer-deps=true
